  "title": "The summer at Lake Wren",
  "year": 1998,
  "text": "We left before sunrise, the four of us and a cooler that wouldn't close, and Sam was asleep on the sleeping bags before we even reached the highway. The cabin was smaller than the pictures, with one window that stuck and a porch that leaned toward the water, and the kids loved it right away. On the third day David finally got the canoe out, and Maya paddled the whole way across while he pretended he was doing all the work. On our last night we sat on the dock until the stars came out, and nobody wanted to say it was time to go home. David still says the canoe was his idea.",
